# One instance of the colour structure in style.md. Never ship it as is: every game re-chooses
# each role for its own tone. Checked against style.md's colour-rules (value = HSV V,
# chroma = S x V, contrast = WCAG ratio, hue distance in degrees on the HSV wheel):
#   value(void) 0.047 (<= 0.06); value(grid) 0.32, chroma(grid) 0.23 (<= 0.35, <= 0.25)
#   gameplay roles: chroma >= 0.64, value 1.00; contrast on void >= 5.2, on grid >= 3.7
#   player on void 14.5:1; hud-ink on hud-panel 16.4:1, on void 17.4:1; chroma(hud-ink) 0.10
#   hue gaps: enemies/danger to player and core >= 78; enemy pairs >= 49;
#   danger to enemies and pickup >= 33; pickup to enemies >= 36; core to player 36
# Silhouettes (not checkable here): player dart, seeker open triangle, splitter three rings,
